.TH PRINTENV 1.SH NAMEprintenv \- print environment variables.SH SYNOPSIS\fBprintenv\fR[\-a] [name ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBprintenv\fRprints the variables named, or every variable, one to a line as\fBNAME=value\fR.\fRVariables whose names begin with\fB@\fRare left out unless\fB\-a\fRis given; those are the ZSH shell's own.  By Lukas Zeller, 1989..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-a\fRall variables, including the ones beginning with\fB@\fR.\fR.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOgetenv, env